<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonld={jsonld} navVariant="inner">
<section class="hero">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow">Cluster — 72-hour response</span>
<h1>Furniture inspection &amp; supplier verification in Kolkata</h1>
<p class="lead">Cane, rattan and natural-fibre furniture from the eastern belt — Kolkata's furniture manufacturers specialise in natural materials. Every Qualis service is available across the cluster now, with 72-hour response from Jodhpur.</p>
<div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-independent/">Why independent</a></div>
</div>
</section>
<section><div class="wrap"><h2 class="vh">What we inspect in Kolkata</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/defects/"><h3>Material treatment</h3><p>Untreated or under-treated cane invites borer and mould in transit — treatment verification is check one.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/container-loading-supervision/"><h3>Mould in transit</h3><p>Natural fibre plus container humidity: desiccant plans and moisture checks are non-negotiable.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Weave consistency</h3><p>Hand-woven surfaces vary by weaver; sampling breadth matters more here than anywhere.</p></a></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>What Kolkata makes, and why buyers source here</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Kolkata anchors the eastern belt for cane, rattan, seagrass and natural-fibre furniture, often combined with wood frames — the material Western buyers want for conservatory, outdoor and casual ranges, and the material most exposed to the journey out. Natural fibre is organic and hygroscopic in a way solid timber is not: it can carry moisture, it can carry pests, and a hand-woven surface varies weaver to weaver.</p><p class="prose rv">So the defining risks here are biological, and they make pre-shipment and loading checks a pair rather than a choice. Untreated or under-treated cane invites borer and mould in transit, which is why treatment verification is check one; natural fibre sealed into a humid container is how a clean shipment arrives mouldy, which is why a desiccant and moisture plan is non-negotiable; and hand-woven consistency varies more than machine work, which is why sampling breadth matters more in Kolkata than almost anywhere.</p></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Pre-Shipment Inspection</h3><p>AQL 2.5, moisture, structure, finish vs golden sample — report in 24h.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/supplier-verification-india/"><h3>Supplier Verification</h3><p>Unannounced premises visits, verdict in 3–5 working days.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/factory-audit-india/"><h3>Factory Audit</h3><p>8-section scored audit for programme onboarding.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/container-loading-supervision/"><h3>Container Loading Supervision</h3><p>Tally, dunnage, weather hold and photographed seal.</p></a></div></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>How Qualis covers Kolkata</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Kolkata is the furthest cluster from our Jodhpur base, covered on a 72-hour response — a planned, on-the-ground visit rather than a remote sign-off. The sequence that protects a natural-fibre order is verification of treatment and materials up front, a pre-shipment inspection that samples the weave broadly and confirms moisture, and container loading supervision that checks the desiccant and stowage before the doors close. All Qualis services are available, buyer-paid, with the report within 24 hours of the visit.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>Before you order from Kolkata</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Natural-fibre orders are won or lost on a few conditions set before loading. <strong>Require a treatment or fumigation certificate</strong> — untreated or under-treated cane invites borer and mould in transit, so make treatment verification a condition, not an afterthought. <strong>Agree a desiccant and moisture plan before the container is stuffed</strong> — natural fibre plus container humidity is how a clean shipment arrives mouldy, so specify desiccant and a moisture ceiling and check both at loading. <strong>Widen the sampling for hand-weave</strong> — woven consistency varies weaver to weaver, so agree a larger sample against the golden reference than a machine-made product would need.</p></div></section>
<section class="final">
<div class="wrap">

<h2>Your next India order. Protected.</h2>
<p>Confirmed within 2 hours. Report within 24 hours of inspection. Paid by buyers only — never by factories.</p>
<a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a>
